title: 'skg export-obsidian : exporting a skgrepo as an Obsidian vault'
pid: a8e4e1aa-270e-4a96-8b61-df37b654081f
body: |2-
  :PROPERTIES:
  :CUSTOM_ID: export-obsidian
  :END:
  Writes one owned skgrepo as a vault that Obsidian can open, so that
  the notes can be read without Skg. It needs no server, and no client
  command runs it yet:
  : cargo run --bin skg -- export-obsidian [config-path] [skgrepo] [output-dir]
  (Once built, =bash/skg= runs the binary in place of
  =cargo run --bin skg --=, here and below.)
  =skgrepo= defaults to the config's most public owned skgrepo, and
  =output-dir= (relative to the current directory) to =obsidian-vault=.
  A foreign skgrepo is refused. Only the files of the skgrepo named are
  read, so no text of another skgrepo can reach the vault.
  The output directory must be absent, empty, or a vault an earlier
  export wrote. Files that earlier export wrote and this one does not
  are removed; nothing else there is touched.
  The plan, and how the build departs from it, are in
  =TODO/export-obsidian/=.
